  "status": "PASS exact edge-block recurrence; terminal Hermitian/Gram collapse",
  "terminal_verdict": "The KKT sum is the archived global Euler trace.  The only positive edge-energy refinement is the centered contribution/star-frame SOS, equivalently the [8]+[6,2] perfect-matching incidence Gram sector. It gives a lower bound, not a vanishing summand; equality would make all U_e=Y/7 and therefore makes every contribution visible.  It contains no response-star variables and cannot force a clean cap.",
  "theorem": {
    "N8_energy": "For U_e=T_e(A_e), sum_e U_e=4Y and sum_(e incident v)U_e=Y. Thus for ternary GHZ, sum_e h_e||A_e||^2 = 12/7 + sum_e ||U_e-Y/7||^2.",
    "block_map": "For e=pq and residual matching tensor C_e, T_e(X)=X tensor C_e in endpoint-word order, hence T_e^*T_e=h_e I9, h_e=||C_e||^2.",
    "global_KKT": "A regular global norm minimum obeys A_e=T_e^*lambda. Summing <A_e,A_e>=<lambda,T_eA_e> gives ||A||^2=m<lambda,Y>. The Fritz--John alpha=0 branch supplies no such normalized identity.",
    "least_norm": "Writing Phi(A)=T_e(A_e)+B_e, a fibre norm minimum has A_e=0 when h_e=0.  When h_e!=0, A_e=h_e^(-1)T_e^*(Y-B_e); because Y-B_e=T_e(A_e), this visible-chart formula is tautological."
  }
